Brand logos
-----------

The 121 logos in src/assets/logos/ and mobile/src/app/assets/logos/ are
trademarks (and, for some, copyrighted artwork) of their owners. They are NOT
covered by the GPL or by any licence in this repository. They are shown only
to identify the user's own accounts in the user's own vault, and no
endorsement by, or affiliation with, any owner is implied. Anyone
redistributing KAPEVault is responsible for their own use of these marks and
may remove any of them: a brand without a logo shows the normal letter tile.

Where each came from, as recorded per logo in src/features/brands/brands.json
(a "source" key; scripts/fetch-logos.mjs downloads the first three kinds):

- 76 from svgl (https://svgl.app). The svgl code is MIT, which says nothing
  about the logos: svgl hosts each owner's artwork without granting rights to
  it, and asks its contributors to make sure they may use what they add.
- 21 from Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org). Its icon data is CC0-1.0, but
  its DISCLAIMER says that does not mean every icon is CC0 or free of
  trademark rights.
- 5 downloaded from the brand's own website: Apify and CIMB (an icon file the
  site serves) and Kie, Lightspeed and Blotato (the icon the site declares).
- 19 cut, recoloured or drawn here ("source": local):
  - 10 from Wikimedia Commons file pages whose status there is public domain
    (simple shapes) with a trademark restriction: GCash, SeaBank, BDO,
    Metrobank, UnionBank, PNB, Security Bank, China Bank, EastWest Bank,
    Payoneer.
  - 5 from the brand's own website: Maya, GoTyme, BPI, RCBC, M Lhuillier.
  - Wise: the Simple Icons mark, recoloured. GoHighLevel: cut from the SVG on
    their website.
  - Palawan Express and Cebuana Lhuillier: drawn here to look like the mark.
    There is no source file.

Logos of Philippine government agencies (SSS, PhilHealth, Pag-IBIG Fund, BIR)
and two taken from non-free uploads on the English Wikipedia (Landbank,
Remitly) were removed before the first release. These six brands are shown
by name only, with no logo: they stay in the catalog ("logo": false in
brands.json), so they are still offered and still recognised by name, and
they show a letter tile. A government agency's mark is not ours to ship in a paid product without
its approval, and KAPEVault Pro is a paid product.
